      <h2 class="ll-why__headline">Philadelphia's Aging Glass Stock Needs a Film That Works in Every Season</h2>
      <p class="ll-why__intro">
        Zone 4A puts Philadelphia glass under pressure from both directions — peak summer solar gain drives commercial cooling costs, and cold winters expose the energy loss in the city's large stock of aging single-pane rowhome glass. LLumar addresses both in one lineup: the ATC Series cuts summer solar heat gain through commercial glazing without sacrificing daylight, while Low-E film adds winter insulation performance to residential glass that predates double-pane technology. For a mixed-humid city where the HVAC system works hard in July and heating bills spike in January, that two-season range is the practical reason LLumar is the specified product on Philadelphia commercial and residential projects.
      </p>
