      <p style="font-family:var(--font-body,'DM Sans',sans-serif);font-size:15px;color:var(--text-mid,#4a4a4a);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 18px;">Zone 4A puts Philadelphia glass under pressure from both directions — peak summer solar gain drives commercial cooling costs, and cold winters expose the energy loss in the city's large stock of aging single-pane glass. LLumar addresses both in one lineup: the ATC Series cuts summer heat gain through commercial glazing while Low-E adds winter insulation to residential glass that predates double-pane technology.</p>
