      <span class="ll-pl-row__eyebrow">LLumar Low-E Climate Control Window Film</span>
      <h3 class="ll-pl-row__heading">Low-E Series — Year-Round Insulation for Philadelphia's Four Seasons</h3>
      <p class="ll-pl-row__body">LLumar Low-E is a dual-season low-emissivity film engineered to work in both directions. In summer, it rejects solar heat gain. In winter, it reflects interior warmth back into the room instead of allowing it to escape through the glass. The result is a window that performs closer to double-pane insulated glass without window replacement — meaningful for Philadelphia's large stock of aging single-pane rowhome glass.</p>
      <p class="ll-pl-row__body">LLumar Low-E maintains 74% visible light transmission and reads as clear glass from inside and out. With just 15% exterior reflectance, it stays within the guidelines of Philadelphia's historic neighborhood HOAs in Germantown, Chestnut Hill, and Society Hill. For commercial-scale specifications across multiple floors, see our <a href="/applications/office/" class="ll-body-link">commercial office window film</a> page.</p>

